  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.5.0: TechTeaStudio.Billing.Abstractions additionally targets netstandard2.0 and net472, so .NET Framework 4.6.2+ assemblies can share the contracts. This package itself stays .NET 5+ - it needs the ASP.NET Core shared framework, which has not run on .NET Framework since ASP.NET Core 3.0.\n\nv0.4.0: Targets net5.0 through net10.0 (was net8.0+). Contracts split into the dependency-free TechTeaStudio.Billing.Abstractions package, pulled in automatically - namespaces are unchanged, so existing code compiles as-is. Webhook endpoints now map through RequestDelegate instead of minimal-API lambdas, which is what makes net5.0/net6.0 possible; behaviour and status codes are identical. Symbol packages, SourceLink and package validation added.\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/TechTeaStudio/Billing/blob/product/CHANGELOG.md",
